meta {
  name: Move Invited Speaker to CONTACTED (PR 11 — bridge to /promote)
  type: http
  seq: 1.3
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/events/{{speakerPortalTestEventCode}}/speakers/{{invitedSpeakerPoolId}}/status
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "newStatus": "CONTACTED",
    "reason": "PR 11 — bridge transition before promote-to-READY"
  }
}

tests {
  test("transitions invite speaker IDENTIFIED → CONTACTED for promote bridge", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.currentStatus).to.equal('CONTACTED');
  });
}

docs {
  PR 11 cascade fix: ADR-009 §0.1 requires CONTACTED → READY → INVITED, with READY
  reachable only via POST /promote. Pre-Epic-11 the invite-speaker endpoint left the
  speaker at IDENTIFIED or INVITED and the /send-invitation endpoint was the only
  hop; test 02 (send-invitation-email) worked because the speaker_pool.username was
  populated at IDENTIFIED time and the legacy `findByUsername` lookup succeeded.

  Post-Epic-11 (Story 11.E.9), speaker_pool no longer carries username — the
  canonical identity lives on session_users, created at READY time. So the
  /send-invitation lookup-by-username fails (404) until the speaker reaches READY.
  This bridge step + 01b-promote drives the speaker to READY before test 02 runs.
}
